<title>USA: Syscomm cuts IPO pricing terms.</title>
<headline>Syscomm cuts IPO pricing terms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syscomm International Corp cut terms of its proposed initial public offering to 1.5 million shares to price between $5 to $5.50 each, according to a regulatory filing.</p>
<p>The offering is due to price Monday for trading Tuesday according to lead underwriter Commonwealth Associates. The company integrates systems and resells computer drilling services. It initially filed for an offering of 1.6 million shares to price between $6 and $8 a share.</p>
<p>The company is based in Hauppauge, New York.</p>
